# Vault Project Context & Guidelines

## 1. Project Overview
- **Name**: Vault (Institutional Cryptographic Custody & Digital Asset Treasury)
- **Live URL**: https://dima3939.github.io/vault/
- **GitHub Repository**: https://github.com/Dima3939/vault
- **Local Directory**: `D:\OpenServer\home\vault`

## 2. Architecture & Technology Stack
- **Frontend**: React 19, TypeScript (Strict Mode), Vite, D3.js (v7), Tailwind CSS / Custom Swiss FinTech Tokens, Lucide Icons, Lenis Smooth Scroll, Canvas Confetti.
- **Backend**: Node.js, Express API, JSON waitlist storage (`backend/waitlist.json`).
- **Deployment**: GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) building to GitHub Pages with `base: '/vault/'`.

## 3. Key Feature Specifications
- **Interactive D3 MPC Visualizer**: Real-time 3-of-5 threshold cryptographic key signing ceremony with dynamic node physics and ECDSA DER payload outputs.
- **Interactive D3 Treasury Flow**: Dynamic multi-chain asset allocation bar and liquidity chart with hover analytics.
- **Programmable Policy Engine**: Toggleable institutional rule governance matrix.
- **Dual Theme Engine**: Titanium Obsidian (`dark`) & Swiss White Banking (`light`) with persistence in `localStorage`.
- **6-Language i18n**: English (`EN`), Ukrainian (`UA`), German (`DE`), Spanish (`ES`), French (`FR`), Russian (`RU`) in an adaptive dropdown menu.
- **Developer SDK Hub**: Copy-ready code snippets for TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust, and cURL.

## 4. Code & Contribution Rules
- **Language & Comments**: All code comments, variable names, documentation, and commit messages must be strictly in **English**.
- **Discretion**: Zero mentions of AI generation, prompts, or LLMs in source code, commits, or client-facing metadata.
